From: fp5-touch <local>
Subject: [PATCH] dbus/ei: allow org.tideshell.Shell to open an EI sender socket

tideshell's virtual trackpad sends relative pointer motion, buttons and scroll
through cosmic-comp's EI path, the same way cosmic-osk does. GetSenderSocket
only accepts callers that own an allowlisted well-known name; add the shell's.
Trust level is the same as the existing CosmicOSK entry.

Base: cosmic-comp epoch-1.8.0. Type-checked with rustc 1.91
(--ignore-rust-version) on x86_64; not run on hardware.
---
diff --git a/src/dbus/ei.rs b/src/dbus/ei.rs
index 263bced4..e6f6a21c 100644
--- a/src/dbus/ei.rs
+++ b/src/dbus/ei.rs
@@ -11,6 +11,9 @@ use super::name_owners::NameOwners;
 static ALLOWED_NAMES: &[WellKnownName] = &[
     WellKnownName::from_static_str_unchecked("org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.cosmic"),
     WellKnownName::from_static_str_unchecked("com.system76.CosmicOSK"),
+    // tideshell's virtual trackpad (relative pointer + buttons + scroll).
+    // Same trust level as CosmicOSK: owning a session-bus name.
+    WellKnownName::from_static_str_unchecked("org.tideshell.Shell"),
 ];
 
 /// Channel for handing the EI socketpair (and requested device types)
